  "declared_deviations_from_published_nrms": [
    "The news encoder is a linear projection of A1's pinned sentence embeddings (multilingual-e5-small, 384-d) rather than learned word embeddings with word-level self-attention. See a2_q3_plan.md for the three reasons.",
    "Hyperparameters are our declared choices, not the paper's or ebnerd-benchmark's \u2014 neither has been read (OQ-12).",
    "The user encoder is permutation-invariant over the click history, as published NRMS is: attention without positional encoding is a set operation. A1's 'recency' pooling used order; this architecture cannot express it."
  ],
  "graded_comparison": "delta_vs_reproduction on nrms_category_aware \u2014 the only comparison that isolates the one principled change (A2.Q3.3, A2.Q3.4). A delta whose interval contains zero is established: false, and no improvement is claimed.",
